From c0c7b065e9cab4f5c3fccb4f920a42342650cbc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex-acsit <alex@acsit.com.au>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:22:41 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] MisterOperator kiosk support

While /tmp/kiosk_active exists (created by the MisterOperator kiosk while
it owns the screen):
- the menu core goes straight to the Linux framebuffer instead of showing
  the MiSTer menu (no stock-menu flash at boot or after a game);
- the OSD can't be opened and OSD hotkeys are ignored;
- volume changes don't pop up the OSD volume bar.
Without the file, behaviour is unchanged.

Adds a save_nvram MiSTer_cmd command that saves an arcade core's NVRAM
without opening the OSD, and lists these features in /tmp/MiSTer_features
at start-up. Adds a GitHub Actions workflow that builds with the official
ARM GCC 10.2 toolchain.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BiX7tJ3KvN3UYXpZzAPMyh
