new file mode 100644
index 0000000..50fb42e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README_KIOSK.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Main_MiSTer for MisterOperator
+
+This is [Main_MiSTer](https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Main_MiSTer) with a small patch
+for the [MisterOperator](https://github.com/alex-acsit/MisterOperator) arcade kiosk.
+It changes nothing unless the kiosk is running.
+
+While the kiosk is in charge, it creates `/tmp/kiosk_active`, and this build then:
+
+- **never shows the MiSTer menu.** The menu core goes straight to the screen the kiosk
+  draws on, at boot and after every game, with no flash of the stock menu.
+- **can't open the OSD,** and the OSD hotkeys (F12, F1, F9...) are ignored. The kiosk's
+  operator menu removes the flag when the operator asks for the stock MiSTer menu.
+- **doesn't pop up the OSD volume bar.** The kiosk shows the volume itself.
+
+It also adds a `save_nvram` command (`echo save_nvram > /dev/MiSTer_cmd`), which saves the
+running arcade game's NVRAM without opening the OSD. At start-up it lists its extra
+features in `/tmp/MiSTer_features`, so the kiosk knows to use them.
+
+The menu that appears over a running game (when opened from the operator menu's "Game
+settings" or "MiSTer menu") keeps each core's own OSD colour, because that colour is
+built into every core's FPGA design.
+
+## Files changed
+
+`kiosk.cpp` and `kiosk.h` are new. `main.cpp`, `menu.cpp`, `input.cpp` and `audio.cpp` have
+a few lines each, marked with "kiosk" comments. Run `git diff upstream/master` to see the
+whole patch.
+
+## Getting the binary
+
+Every push builds `MiSTer` with the official ARM GCC 10.2 toolchain (GitHub Actions →
+**Build MiSTer** → artifact). Tagged versions attach it to a GitHub release.
+
+## Installing
+
+1. Copy `MiSTer` over `/media/fat/MiSTer` on the SD card (keep the old one as
+   `MiSTer.orig`), then reboot.
+2. Stop the updater replacing it: in `/media/fat/downloader.ini`, set the
+   `[distribution_mister]` section to skip the main binary, or skip updates on the
+   cabinet and update by hand.
+3. To go back to stock MiSTer, copy `MiSTer.orig` back.
+
+## Keeping up with upstream
+
+```
+git remote add upstream https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Main_MiSTer
+git fetch upstream
+git rebase upstream/master     # the patch is small, so conflicts are rare
+git push --force-with-lease
+```
